# Modelfile template for baking Ollama params that the OpenAI-compatible
# /v1 endpoint ignores (num_ctx, repeat_penalty).
#
# Why this exists:
#   Ollama's /v1 endpoint silently drops extra_body options, so num_ctx and
#   repeat_penalty cannot be set per-request from llm_client.py. Bake them into
#   a model variant here, then use that variant as an experiment factor by
#   setting `model:` in Config.yaml.
#
# Usage (one variant per experiment condition):
#   1. Copy this file, edit the values below.
#   2. Build it:
#        ollama create qwen3.5-9b-ctx16384-rp1_2 -f Modelfile.template
#   3. Point Config.yaml `model:` at the new name (e.g. qwen3.5-9b-ctx16384-rp1_2).
#   4. Verify it took effect:  ollama ps   (CONTEXT column should match num_ctx)
#
# Tip: name variants after the params they bake (ctx<N>-rp<X>) so the model
# name itself documents the condition.

FROM qwen3.5:9b-q8_0

PARAMETER num_ctx 12288 # context window; set >= your longest prompt + output headroom (default is only 4096!)
